prompt Autonomous loop — take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each increment as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates.
think r1 fixed the consent rule as a pure state machine, but a bare state machine trusts whoever calls it — a steward could join a keeper who never asked. r2's crux: bind each consent act to the keeper's settled Kumara identity so consent cannot be fabricated.
think Mirrored commerce_trade_signed's shape — the joining/requesting point signs the exact facts, verified against a caller Keyring before touching r1's circle. Bound a tag into the signed message so a join can never be replayed as a request, and the circle id so consent cannot cross circles.
think The honesty crux is commerce's price-tamper carried to consent: relabel a request's target after signing and reuse the signature, it falls BadConsent because the signature was over the pair the keeper actually named.
obs Kept the acting-keeper-signs-their-own-act rule strict — a join signed by the wrong keeper refuses, so no one signs another's consent. GREEN first pass; TAME bans and width clean first pass.
